[116.789932, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\n# Post-Compromise Intrusion Report\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nOn host `smb-prod-01`, an external threat actor executed a multi-stage compromise sequence originating from IP `198.51.100.218` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). The intrusion exploited an unpatched SMBv1 vulnerability (CVE-2017-0144 / MS17-010) in `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/sas/baseline.json`), dropping an initial DoublePulsar-class exploit implant at `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/sas/alerts.json`). The threat actor subsequently executed PowerShell scripts, dumped LSASS process memory to `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` (`/sas/alerts.json`), and deployed a ransomware binary at `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` (`/sas/alerts.json`).\n\nWhile primary execution and impact activities generated endpoint alerts, the threat actor established silent persistence and evasion mechanisms that were NOT captured by security alerting feeds:\n1. **WMI Event Subscription Persistence** (`T1546.003`): An `__EventFilter` bound to a `CommandLineEventConsumer` recorded in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`).\n2. **DLL Search-Order Hijacking** (`T1574.001`): A malicious `wbemcomn.dll` placed in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\n3. **Anti-Forensic Log Clearing** (`T1070.001`): Wiping of the System event log (EventID 1102) recorded in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`).\n\n---\n\n## 2. Threat Actor Entities & Infrastructure\n- **Source IP**: `198.51.100.218` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)\n- **C2 Domain**: `update-smb.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)\n- **Mining Pool / C2 Channel**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.smb.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`)\n- **Monero Wallet Address**: `4A000000000000000000c814c46d6253` (`/s"]
[116.789964, "i", "as/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Detailed Attack Chain & ATT&CK Mapping\n\n### Step 1: Exploitation of Remote Services (T1210)\n- **Description**: Threat actor targeted unpatched SMBv1 service (`srv.sys`) using EternalBlue (CVE-2017-0144).\n- **Implant Binary**: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`).\n- **Alert ID**: `ALERT-01` (`/sas/alerts.json`).\n- **Status**: Alerted.\n\n### Step 2: PowerShell Execution (T1059.001)\n- **Description**: Attacker executed PowerShell commands to conduct post-exploitation activities and stage payloads.\n- **Evidence**: Advisory mapping (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`).\n- **Status**: Alerted / Advisory documented.\n\n### Step 3: LSASS Credential Dumping (T1003.001)\n- **Description**: Attacker dumped LSASS memory to extract domain credentials.\n- **Artifact**: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`).\n- **Recovered Artifact**: Credential cache fragment in `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`).\n- **Alert ID**: `ALERT-02` (`/sas/alerts.json`).\n- **Status**: Alerted.\n\n### Step 4: Data Encrypted for Impact (T1486)\n- **Description**: Attacker executed ransomware payload to encrypt host user data files.\n- **Artifact**: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`).\n- **Alert ID**: `ALERT-03` (`/sas/alerts.json`).\n- **Status**: Alerted.\n\n### Step 5: WMI Event Subscription Persistence (T1546.003)\n- **Description**: Attacker established WMI persistence using an `__EventFilter` bound to a `CommandLineEventConsumer` in the WMI repository.\n- **Artifact**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`).\n- **Status**: **SILENT (Unalerted)**.\n\n### Step 6: DLL Search-Order Hijacking (T1574.001)\n- **Description**: Attacker dropped a rogue `wbemcomn.dll` library into the WBEM directory to hijack application DLL search order.\n- **Artifact**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\n- **Status**: **SILENT (Unalerted)**.\n\n### Step 7: Clear Windows Event Logs (T1070.001)\n- **Description**: Attacker cleared the Security/System event logs (EventID 1102) to cover footprints and hinder investigation.\n- **Artifact**: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`).\n- **Status**: **SILENT (Unalerted)**.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Alerted vs. Silent Activity Matrix\n\n| ATT&CK Technique | Description | Artifact Path | Alert Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `T1210` | SMBv1 EternalBlue Exploit | `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` | Alerted (`ALERT-01`, `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| `T1059.001` | PowerShell Execution | System PowerShell | Documented (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`) |\n| `T1003.001` | LSASS Memory Dump | `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` | Alerted (`ALERT-02`, `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| `T1486` | Ransomware Binary | `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` | Alerted (`ALERT-03`, `/sas/alerts.json`) |\n| `T1546.003` | WMI Event Subscription | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` | **SILENT** |\n| `T1574.001` | DLL Search-Order Hijack | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` | **SILENT** |\n| `T1070.001` | System Log Clear | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` | **SILENT** |\nEOF\n"]
[116.792077, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/intrusion-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # Post-Compromise Intrusion Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## 1. Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> On host `smb-prod-01`, an external threat actor executed a multi-stage compromise sequence originating from IP `198.51.100.218` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`). The intrusion exploited an unpatched SMBv1 vulnerability (CVE-2017-0144 / MS17-010) in `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/sas/baseline.json`), dropping an initial DoublePulsar-class exploit implant at `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/sas/alerts.json`). The threat actor subsequently executed PowerShell scripts, dumped LSASS process memory to `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` (`/sas/alerts.json`), and deployed a ransomware binary at `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` (`/sas/alerts.json`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> While primary execution and impact activities generated endpoint alerts, the threat actor established silent persistence and evasion mechanisms that were NOT captured by security alerting feeds:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 1. **WMI Event Subscription Persistence** (`T1546.003`): An `__EventFilter` bound to a `CommandLineEventConsumer` recorded in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 2. **DLL Search-Order Hijacking** (`T1574.001`): A malicious `wbemcomn.dll` placed in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> 3. **Anti-Forensic Log Clearing** (`T1070.001`): Wiping of the System event log (EventID 1102) recorded in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## 2. Threat Actor Entities & Infrastructure\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Source IP**: `198.51.100.218` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **C2 Domain**: `update-smb.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Mining Pool / C2 Channel**: `stratum+tcp://xmr.smb.evil:3333` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Monero Wallet Address**: `4A000000000000000000c814c46d6253` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[116.7921, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
