[129.15409, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/vuln-report.md\n# Vulnerability-Driven Entry Analysis Report\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nThe initial entry vector for the compromise of host `smb-prod-01` was the exploitation of the legacy Server Message Block Version 1 (SMBv1) protocol driver `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/sas/baseline.json`, `/sas/alerts.json`). The vulnerability exploited was **CVE-2017-0144** (commonly associated with MS17-010 / EternalBlue / DoublePulsar), which allowed remote unauthenticated arbitrary code execution at the SYSTEM level.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Vulnerability Assessment & Details\n\n- **CVE Identifier**: CVE-2017-0144 (`/sas/vulns.json`, `/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\n- **Severity**: CVSS 8.8 HIGH (v3.1) (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`)\n- **Target Service / Component**: Microsoft Windows SMBv1 Server (`srv.sys`) located at `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`)\n- **Exploit Methodology**: Remote code execution via buffer handling vulnerability in SMBv1 request processing.\n- **Observed Post-Exploitation Implant**: DoublePulsar-class SMB exploit implant dropped at `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json`).\n\n---\n\n## 3. Discrepancy & Verification Notes\n- **Reconciliation with Initial Ticket Draft**: Change ticket draft (`/sas/handoff/change-ticket.md`) incorrectly listed **CVE-2019-0708 (BlueKeep)** targeting RDP. System log examination and threat intelligence confirm that BlueKeep was **NOT** used in this intrusion.\n- **Confirmed Entry Vector**: All on-disk artifacts and threat intelligence (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/sas/vulns.json`) consistently confirm **CVE-2017-0144 (EternalBlue)** via SMBv1 (`srv.sys`).\nEOF\n"]
