[143.443035, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\n# Baseline and Configuration Weaknesses Report\n\n## 1. Executive Summary\nAnalysis of target host `smb-prod-01` identified significant baseline vulnerabilities, legacy configuration risks, and missing security controls that enabled initial compromise, persistence, and defense evasion.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Identified Configuration & Baseline Weaknesses\n\n### 1. Legacy SMBv1 Enabled (Check: `CHK-07`, Capability: `BAS-01`)\n- **Finding**: SMBv1 protocol driver `srv.sys` is enabled and active.\n- **Risk**: Legacy SMBv1 protocol lacks modern security controls and is vulnerable to unauthenticated remote code execution.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`), `/sas/baseline.json` (`/sas/baseline.json`), `/sas/alerts.json` (`/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-04]).\n\n### 2. Missing Security Patch MS17-010\n- **Finding**: Operating system lacks cumulative update patching CVE-2017-0144 for `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`.\n- **Risk**: Allows attackers to execute arbitrary code via malformed SMBv1 packets.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`), `/sas/vulns.json` (`/sas/vulns.json`).\n\n### 3. Unrestricted System Temp & Public Executable Directories\n- **Finding**: Attacker was able to write and execute binaries in `/disk/Windows/Temp` and `/disk/Users/Public`.\n- **Risk**: Staging and execution of unauthorized binaries without AppLocker / Software Restriction Policy enforcement.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`), `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`), `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`).\n\n### 4. Absence of WMI Repository Auditing & Integrity Monitoring\n- **Finding**: Attacker created persistence via WMI event filter/consumer in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` without triggering any security alerts.\n- **Risk**: Stealthy persistence via WMI event subscriptions remains undetected by legacy antivirus/EDR.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`).\n\n### 5. Insecure DLL Search-Order Handling\n- **Finding**: Rogue `wbemcomn.dll` placed in WBEM directory (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\n- **Risk**: Arbitrary DLL execution when system utilities load libraries.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\n\n### 6. Insufficient Auditing for Event Log Tampering\n- **Finding**: Security event log cleared (EventID 1102) in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` without generating a real-time security alert.\n- **Risk**: Impairment of DFIR visibility and loss of forensic history.\n- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`).\nEOF\n"]
[143.443978, "o", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/baseline-report.md\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> # Baseline and Configuration Weaknesses Report\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## 1. Executive Summary\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> Analysis of target host `smb-prod-01` identified significant baseline vulnerabilities, legacy configuration risks, and missing security controls that enabled initial compromise, persistence, and defense evasion.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ---\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ## 2. Identified Configuration & Baseline Weaknesses\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 1. Legacy SMBv1 Enabled (Check: `CHK-07`, Capability: `BAS-01`)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Finding**: SMBv1 protocol driver `srv.sys` is enabled and active.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.444466, "o", "- **Risk**: Legacy SMBv1 protocol lacks modern security controls and is vulnerable to unauthenticated remote code execution.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.44484, "o", "- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`), `/sas/baseline.json` (`/sas/baseline.json`), `/sas/alerts.json` (`/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-04]).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.44493, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[143.444994, "o", "> "]
[143.445009, "o", "\r\n"]
[143.445053, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.44551, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[143.44612, "o", "> "]
[143.446333, "o", "### 2. Missing Security Patch MS17-010\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.446437, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.446825, "o", "- **Finding**: Operating system lacks cumulative update patching CVE-2017-0144 for `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.446879, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[143.447021, "o", "> "]
[143.447295, "o", "- **Risk**: Allows attackers to execute arbitrary code via malformed SMBv1 packets.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.447387, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[143.447427, "o", "> "]
[143.447645, "o", "- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`), `/sas/vulns.json` (`/sas/vulns.json`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.447681, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n"]
[143.447696, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.447788, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.447884, "o", "### 3. Unrestricted System Temp & Public Executable Directories\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.447907, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[143.447966, "o", "> "]
[143.448138, "o", "- **Finding**: Attacker was able to write and execute binaries in `/disk/Windows/Temp` and `/disk/Users/Public`.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[143.448187, "o", "> "]
[143.448326, "o", "- **Risk**: Staging and execution of unauthorized binaries without AppLocker / Software Restriction Policy enforcement.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.448371, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.448657, "o", "- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`), `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`), `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.448758, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.448808, "o", "### 4. Absence of WMI Repository Auditing & Integrity Monitoring\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.448874, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.449191, "o", "- **Finding**: Attacker created persistence via WMI event filter/consumer in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` without triggering any security alerts.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.44933, "o", "- **Risk**: Stealthy persistence via WMI event subscriptions remains undetected by legacy antivirus/EDR.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.449476, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.449612, "o", "- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.449737, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.449767, "o", "### 5. Insecure DLL Search-Order Handling\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.449943, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.450022, "o", "- **Finding**: Rogue `wbemcomn.dll` placed in WBEM directory (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.450106, "o", "\u001b[?2004h"]
[143.450117, "o", "> "]
[143.450218, "o", "- **Risk**: Arbitrary DLL execution when system utilities load libraries.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.450284, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.450893, "o", "- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> ### 6. Insufficient Auditing for Event Log Tampering\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Finding**: Security event log cleared (EventID 1102) in `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` without generating a real-time security alert.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> - **Risk**: Impairment of DFIR visibility and loss of forensic history.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[143.451078, "o", "- **Evidence Citation**: `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`).\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> EOF\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[143.45183, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@ca5d1b5317d6:/app# "]
[157.849072, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /sas/handoff/change-ticket.md\n# CHANGE TICKET  CHG-1677  (RECONCILED)\n\n> Reconciled against forensic findings on `/disk` and SAS threat telemetry (`/sas`).\n\n| # | Action | Target | Status | Note | Citation |\n|---|--------|--------|--------|------|----------|\n| 1 | Block source IP inbound | 198.51.100.218 | proposed | Corrected IP from stale 203.0.113.9 to actual threat actor IP | `/sas/cti/advisory.txt` |\n| 2 | Patch CVE-2017-0144 (MS17-010 EternalBlue) and disable SMBv1 | /disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys | proposed | Corrected CVE from BlueKeep (CVE-2019-0708) to CVE-2017-0144 | `/sas/vulns.json` |\n| 3 | Verify cron miner absence on Windows host | /var/spool/cron/root | VERIFIED-REJECTED | Host is Windows; Linux cron path does not exist on host image | `/disk` |\n| 4 | Quarantine and purge WMI Event Subscription persistence | /disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA | proposed | Silent persistence via WMI __EventFilter / CommandLineEventConsumer | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` |\n| 5 | Quarantine hijacked DLL | /disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll | proposed | Silent search-order hijacked DLL payload | `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` |\n| 6 | Quarantine exploit implant | /disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe | proposed | DoublePulsar-class SMB exploit implant | `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` |\n| 7 | Quarantine credential dump file | /disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp | proposed | LSASS memory dump file residue | `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` |\n| 8 | Quarantine ransomware payload | /disk/Users/Public/enc.exe | proposed | Ransomware executable payload | `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` |\n| 9 | Force password reset for compromised accounts | Administrator account | proposed | Credential dump mitigation for cached Administrator credentials | `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak` |\n| 10 | Restore and re-enable Windows Event Log auditing | /disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx | proposed | Anti-forensic log clearing remediation and audit policy enforcement | `/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx` |\n\n## Reviewer checklist\n- [x] Every action maps to a cited artifact under /disk or /sas\n- [x] Fix the wrong IP (row 1) and wrong CVE (row 2)\n- [x] Downgrade row 3 from DONE to VERIFIED-or-OPEN with evidence\n- [x] Add the silent (non-alerted) artifacts the prior shift missed\nEOF\n"]
