[176.002681, "i", "cat << 'EOF' > /app/remediation-plan.md\n# Incident Remediation Plan\n\n## 1. Executive Strategy & Principles\nThis remediation plan outlines the prioritized containment, eradication, recovery, and hardening steps for host `smb-prod-01`. Per DFIR principles:\n- **Isolation & Quarantine**: Malicious binaries, payloads, and persistence artifacts are backed up / quarantined to secure storage rather than deleted.\n- **Evidence Alignment**: Every remediation action corresponds to verified forensic evidence in `/disk` or `/sas`.\n- **Verification**: Each step includes specific validation criteria to confirm successful execution.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Phase-by-Phase Remediation Actions\n\n### Phase 1: Immediate Network Containment\n- **Action 1.1**: Block inbound and outbound communication for C2 IP `198.51.100.218` on perimeter firewalls.\n  - *Target*: Host IP `198.51.100.218` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)\n  - *Verification*: `netsh advfirewall firewall show rule name=Block_Attacker_IP` or firewall policy audit.\n- **Action 1.2**: Block C2 domain `update-smb.example.cn` at DNS sinkhole / egress filtering controls.\n  - *Target*: Domain `update-smb.example.cn` (`/sas/cti/advisory.txt`, `/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`)\n  - *Verification*: DNS query lookup test returning sinkhole IP.\n\n### Phase 2: Host Eradication & Quarantine (Backup over Deletion)\n- **Action 2.1**: Quarantine exploit implant `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` into secure encrypted archive before removal.\n  - *Target*: `/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/mssecsvc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-01])\n  - *Verification*: Confirm binary moved to quarantine directory and absent from system temp.\n- **Action 2.2**: Quarantine LSASS memory dump file `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`.\n  - *Target*: `/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp` (`/disk/Windows/Temp/lsass.dmp`, `/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-02])\n  - *Verification*: Confirm dump file secured in quarantine and removed from temp location.\n- **Action 2.3**: Quarantine ransomware executable `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`.\n  - *Target*: `/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe` (`/disk/Users/Public/enc.exe`, `/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-03])\n  - *Verification*: Confirm binary removed from `/Users/Public` and cataloged in quarantine inventory.\n- **Action 2.4**: Neutralize silent WMI persistence in `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`.\n  - *Target*: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/Repository/OBJECTS.DATA`)\n  - *Command*: Execute `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\\subscription -ClassName __EventFilter | Remove-CimInstance` and `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\\subscription -ClassName CommandLineEventConsumer | Remove-CimInstance` via PowerShell.\n  - *Verification*: `Get-CimInstance -Namespace root\\subscription` returns no suspicious consumers or filters.\n- **Action 2.5**: Quarantine hijacked DLL `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`.\n  - *Target*: `/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll` (`/disk/Windows/System32/wbem/wbemcomn.dll`)\n  - *Verification*: Verify file moved to quarantine; replace with authentic Microsoft signed DLL if required by system.\n\n### Phase 3: Vulnerability Patching & System Hardening\n- **Action 3.1**: Disable legacy SMBv1 protocol system-wide.\n  - *Target*: `/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys` (`/disk/Windows/System32/drivers/srv.sys`, `/sas/baseline.json` [CHK-07])\n  - *Command*: PowerShell `Disable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol -NoRestart` / Registry `Set-ItemProperty -Path \"HKLM:\\SYSTEM\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanServer\\Parameters\" SMB1 -Type DWORD 0 -Force`.\n  - *Verification*: PowerShell `Get-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName SMB1Protocol` shows State: Disabled.\n- **Action 3.2**: Apply Security Update MS17-010 (CVE-2017-0144 patching).\n  - *Target*: Operating system kernel / SMB drivers (`/sas/vulns.json`)\n  - *Verification*: Windows Update status check confirms MS17-010 / KB4012212 (or cumulative equivalent) installation.\n\n### Phase 4: Creden"]
[176.002747, "i", "tial Invalidation & Identity Recovery\n- **Action 4.1**: Reset credentials for Administrator and all domain accounts with active sessions on host `smb-prod-01`.\n  - *Target*: Administrator and domain accounts (`/disk/Windows/System32/config/RegBack/SECURITY.bak`, `/sas/alerts.json` [ALERT-02])\n  - *Verification*: Confirm Active Directory password last set timestamp updated; invalidate Kerberos TGT/TGS tickets.\n\n### Phase 5: Anti-Forensics Remediation & Logging Restoration\n- **Action 5.1**: Restore Windows Security/System Event Log service and enforce centralized log shipping.\n  - *Target*: System event logging framework (`/disk/Windows/System32/winevt/Logs/System.evtx`)\n  - *Verification*: Confirm Event Log service active and forwarding Event ID 1102 / 4624 / 4688 to SIEM.\nEOF\n"]
